<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Murad Giray</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1678">1678</a>–<a href="/years/1683">1683</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Murad Giray was khan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a> from 1678 to 1683. He fought for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> against Muscovy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> and led Crimean cavalry in the Ottoman campaign against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in 1683. After the defeat there, the Ottoman government blamed him for the disaster and deposed him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/murad-giray.jpg" alt="Murad Giray" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jakob Koppmayer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Murad_Giray.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
